<title>BOTSWANA: Metsef reports flat year results.</title>
<headline>Metsef reports flat year results.</headline>
<dateline>GABORONE 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr ended October 31, 1996</p>
<p>			(million pula unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (thebe)		  645    vs     580</p>
<p>    Final dividend (thebe)    20    vs	20</p>
<p>	Making for the year     36    vs	35</p>
<p>    Attrib income	    17.51    vs   18.28</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		    23.01    vs   24.28</p>
<p>    Tax			   5.50    vs    6.01</p>
<p>    Turnover		  543.80    vs  493.60</p>
<p>Div payable first week February 1997</p>
<p>On register January 17, 1997</p>
<p>Full name: Metro Sefalana Cash and Carry Limited</p>
<p>NOTE - The directors said that stringent financial discipline and ongoing improvements in operating efficiences should contribute towards improved margins during the current year by helping to contain expenses and shrinkage.</p>
<p>Metsef is a merger of interests of Sefalana Botswana and Metro Cash and Carry South Africa.</p>
</text>
